# Declarations

## Ethics approval and consent to participate {#decl-ethics}

[PLACEHOLDER: Name the ethics committee and the approval number, and say how consent was obtained or why it was waived. Write "Not applicable." if the study involved no human participants, human data or animals.]

## Consent for publication {#decl-consent-publication}

[PLACEHOLDER: State that consent to publish was obtained if the article contains identifiable personal data or images; otherwise write "Not applicable."]

## Availability of data and materials {#decl-data}

[PLACEHOLDER: Say where the data can be accessed (repository and identifier, or on request) and any restrictions.]

## Code availability {#decl-code}

[PLACEHOLDER: Give the code repository and version, or say how the code can be obtained. Write "Not applicable." if no custom code was used.]

## Competing interests {#decl-competing-interests}

[PLACEHOLDER: List each author's financial and non-financial competing interests as declared by the authors, or write "The authors declare no competing interests."]

## Funding {#decl-funding}

[PLACEHOLDER: List the funders and grant numbers given by the authors and the funders' role, or write "This work received no specific funding."]

## Authors' contributions {#decl-contributions}

[PLACEHOLDER: Each author's contributions as confirmed by the authors (CRediT roles if the journal asks for them).]

## Use of generative AI {#decl-ai}

[PLACEHOLDER: Name any generative AI tools, what they were used for and how the authors checked the output, or write "No generative AI tools were used."]

## Acknowledgements {#decl-acknowledgements}

[PLACEHOLDER: People and institutions who helped but are not authors (with their permission), or write "Not applicable."]

